.TH cargo-cleanme 1 0.2.10 https://github.com/dbowm91/cargo-cleanme "General Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
cargo\-cleanme \- Clean inactive Cargo build artifacts through Cargo, or reconcile the machine read\-only
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcargo\-cleanme\fR [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR] [\fB\-\-stats\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-\-full\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-reclaimable\-bytes\fR] [\fB\-\-older\-than\fR] [\fB\-\-include\fR] [\fB\-\-exclude\fR] [\fB\-\-profile\fR] [\fB\-\-package\fR] [\fB\-\-cargo\-preview\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIROOT\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Clean inactive Cargo build artifacts through Cargo, or reconcile the machine read\-only.
.PP
Bare `cargo cleanme` runs routine maintenance: it selects the maintenance scope (bounded seed roots plus active learned roots plus the working directory, or a configured scan.root when one exists), re\-proves complete ownership for every discovered participant, and executes eligible Cargo cleanup units. The working directory is part of that scope, so a bare run cleans what is under it \-\- and the scope only ever grows, never narrows. `\-\-dry\-run` performs the identical decision and proof path while invoking no `cargo clean` process at all.
.PP
The root is the cleanup front door: `cargo cleanme ROOT` cleans one bounded root, `cargo cleanme \-\-full` runs the Full cleanup \-\- a complete machine reconciliation, then the learned roots it can prove \-\- and `\-\-cargo\-preview` and the policy overrides work here too. A directory whose name collides with a subcommand name is read as that subcommand; spell it `./scan` to name it.
.PP
`cargo cleanme scan` needs a scope: `\-\-all` is the full read\-only machine reconciliation and the only operation allowed to expire learned roots, `scan ROOT` is a bounded explicit scan, and `scan \-\-known` is the read\-only maintenance inventory.
.PP
Deletion is always delegated to Cargo; cargo\-cleanme never removes a directory itself.
.PP
INVOCATION
             After installation the binary is invoked by Cargo as an external
             subcommand, so the supported spelling is:
.PP
             	cargo cleanme [SUBCOMMAND] [OPTIONS]
.PP
             A directly downloaded binary is invoked as
	cargo\-cleanme [SUBCOMMAND] [OPTIONS]
.PP
             Both spellings accept exactly the same arguments.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR
Disable transient progress UI (useful for benchmarks and debugging)
.TP
\fB\-\-stats\fR
Print detailed scan/cleanup counters and phase timings to stderr. Never changes deterministic stdout. `\-\-no\-progress \-\-stats` is the canonical benchmark/debug combination
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: human]
Select human\-readable output, the versioned JSON automation contract, or one bounded ASCII summary line for unattended schedulers
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
log: One bounded ASCII summary line per report, for unattended schedulers that retain a short history tail. Not a machine contract: complete consumers use `json`
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show the detailed human surface: every workspace considered (including the ones that were skipped), the scope census, the per\-phase counters, and the diagnostic detail.

The default surface names only what the run acted on. This flag changes the *human* format only — the JSON document and the log line are identical with and without it.
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Simulate: run every decision, proof, and reporting step, but invoke no `cargo clean` process at all. Honoured wherever it appears, so the `cargo cleanme \-\-dry\-run ROOT` spelling cannot fall back to Execute. Only the cleanup surface (and `update`\*(Aqs own `\-\-dry\-run`) honour it: `scan` and `config` ignore a global `\-\-dry\-run` (read\-only / local\-only, no behaviour change)
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interactive\fR
Choose the workspaces to clean from an inline selection list (NOR/INS).

Resolves the cleanup units read\-only, presents one row per unit with its reclaimable bytes, and cleans only what is checked. A selection can remove candidates but never add one: ownership is still proven across the complete universe and the engine still re\-proves it per spawn.

The list is a bounded page, not the whole screen: PageUp, PageDown, Home and End move through it, and `i` filters it by path.

Requires a terminal on stdin and stdout. Combine with `\-\-dry\-run` to review a selection without invoking `cargo clean`.
.TP
\fB\-\-full\fR
Complete Full reconciliation before cleaning its learned roots.

The canonical spelling of the Full cleanup operation (ADR 008 §4b). `cargo cleanme clean \-\-full` remains accepted as a hidden alias.
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-reclaimable\-bytes\fR \fI<MIN_RECLAIMABLE_BYTES>\fR
Require at least this many reclaimable bytes per workspace
.TP
\fB\-\-older\-than\fR \fI<OLDER_THAN>\fR
Require this many seconds of inactivity
.TP
\fB\-\-include\fR \fI<INCLUDE>\fR
Include canonical workspace roots matching this glob (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-exclude\fR \fI<EXCLUDE>\fR
Exclude canonical workspace roots matching this glob (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fR \fI<PROFILE>\fR
Ask Cargo to clean one named profile. Selector byte estimates are unknown
.TP
\fB\-\-package\fR \fI<PACKAGE>\fR
Clean one validated workspace package through qualified Cargo versions
.TP
\fB\-\-cargo\-preview\fR
Cargo preview: after the same complete final proof, invoke Cargo\*(Aqs own `clean \-\-dry\-run \-\-verbose`. Never removes anything
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fIROOT\fR]
Optional bounded sandbox root. Omit to use the maintenance scope (identical to bare invocation) or select `\-\-full`.

A directory whose name collides with a subcommand name (`scan`, `clean`, `config`, `update`) is read as that subcommand: the subcommand wins. Spell such a directory `./scan` to name it.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
cargo\-cleanme\-scan(1)
Reconcile the machine read\-only: full with `\-\-all`, explicit with ROOT, routine inventory with `\-\-known`
.TP
cargo\-cleanme\-config(1)
.TP
cargo\-cleanme\-update(1)
Update this cargo\-cleanme to the latest stable published release
.SH VERSION
v0.2.10
